{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedWordSurjectivity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedWordSurjectivity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedWordRecovery","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCascadeRightInverse","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedUninsertInvariants","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCascadeColStrict"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L144-L155","doc":"**The form surjectivity wants.** When the run empties the tableau, the word it recovered is a\nword whose insertion tableau is exactly `T`.\n\n`insertWord` is `foldl insert []`, so this is `foldl_insert_uninsertSteps` with the starting\ntableau known to be empty. Whether a given run empties the tableau is a fact about the positions —\nsupplied by the recording tableau, not by anything here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.foldl_insert_uninsertSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.foldl_insert_uninsertSteps","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L123-L142","doc":"**The run's word rebuilds the tableau it was peeled from.**\n\nThe mirror of brick 3's `uninsertSteps_foldl`. That one runs insertions and undoes them; this one\nundoes and re-inserts. Together they make `insertWord` and `uninsertSteps` mutually inverse on\ncolumn-strict tableaux, given the positions.\n\nThe induction is one step of brick 10 (`insert_uninsert`) wrapped around the inductive hypothesis,\nwith bricks 11 and 13 supplying the invariants at the intermediate tableau and brick 13 also ruling\nout the `none` branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_invariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_invariants","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L110-L121","doc":"**The three invariants survive a whole run**, given that every step removes a corner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_cons_snd_some","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_cons_snd_some","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L96-L108","doc":"When a step ejects a value, the run's word gains it at the front. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_cons_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_cons_fst","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**The tableau component of a run does not depend on the `Option`.** Both branches of\n`uninsertSteps`' inner `match` return the same tableau, so a run's tableau is just the composite of\nthe per-step cascades. Isolating this keeps the induction below from case-splitting on an option it\ndoes not care about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_cons","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L78-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_nil","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.CornersAlong","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.CornersAlong","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedWordSurjectivity.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**Every step of the run removes a corner** — of the tableau as it stands at that step, which is\nwhat `ColStrict` preservation needs. Defined by the same recursion as `uninsertSteps`: the later\nsteps of `rest` happen first, so the corner condition for `i` is checked against the tableau they\nleave behind. ","signatureChunk":0}]}